{
  "requirement": "Before that commit, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to revert the drafts the user rejected or deferred and to list them in their report.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has three obligations. The `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents to (1) revert drafts the user rejected or deferred, (2) list those drafts in the report, and (3) do both before the commit.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_reverts_rejected_and_deferred_drafts_before_committing]` carries the `{test}` reference and covers all three.\n- It locates the commit step with `step_of(\"habeas-requirements\", \"all groups together\")`. It then reads that step with `step(...)`. Both go through `workflow_steps`. That helper collapses continuation lines, so the instruction still matches where `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` wraps it across lines.\n- `assert_text_in_order` requires the step to contain \"Revert drafts the user rejected or deferred (`git restore -p`) and list them in your report\". That covers obligations (1) and (2).\n- The same call then requires \"then commit it\" to appear after that phrase, which covers \"before that commit\". The helper panics if either phrase is missing or out of order.\n\nThe test would fail if the skill dropped the revert, dropped the report listing, or moved the revert after the commit. The \"all groups together\" anchor ties the check to the commit step.\n\nThe requirement states no boundary or failure case beyond these. The check is a text assertion on the skill file, so a single scenario is adequate.",
